---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A per-round-trip model of one download. Pick the algorithm, link, buffer, loss and file size and watch cwnd, the transfer time and the queue.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>With the defaults (Reno, 100 Mbit/s, 80 ms RTT, 1 BDP buffer, no loss, 5 MB) the whole transfer takes <b>9 rounds and 811 ms</b>, spends <b>100% of the time in slow start</b> and averages only <b>49.3 Mbit/s</b>. cwnd peaks at 2,560, far above the 684 segment BDP, so the queue adds up to <b>69 ms</b> of delay. The ideal at line rate is 400 ms.</li>
    <li>Set random loss to <b>1%</b>. Reno now needs <b>282 rounds and 23,040 ms</b> (1.7 Mbit/s, 41 retransmissions, 2 timeouts) because every loss halves a small window. Switch to <b>BBR-like</b>: about <b>900 ms</b>. CUBIC is no better than Reno here (about 31 s).</li>
    <li>Choose a <b>50 MB</b> file with no loss: the sawtooth appears (a slow-start overshoot, a halving, then +1 per round), slow start shrinks to <b>19%</b> of the time and the average rises to about <b>90 Mbit/s</b>.</li>
    <li>With the 50 MB file set the buffer to <b>16 x BDP</b>. Reno never loses a packet, so it never backs off: the standing queue adds up to <b>400 ms</b> (bufferbloat) and averages 319 ms. BBR on the same link peaks at 80 ms and averages 10 ms.</li>
    <li>Set the receive window to <b>64 KB</b> with the default file: it takes <b>6,400 ms (6.2 Mbit/s)</b> with Reno, and BBR-like is no better (6,560 ms), because rwnd, not cwnd, is the limit. Drag <b>Round shown</b> to replay the transfer round by round.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg tcp" data-tcp>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Algorithm <select class="pg-in" data-algo><option value="reno" selected>Reno-like AIMD</option><option value="cubic">CUBIC</option><option value="bbr">BBR-like</option></select></label>
      <label>Bandwidth <select class="pg-in" data-mbps><option value="10">10 Mbit/s</option><option value="100" selected>100 Mbit/s</option><option value="1000">1 Gbit/s</option></select></label>
      <label>RTT (ms) <input type="range" min="10" max="300" step="10" value="80" data-rtt /> <b data-rttval>80</b></label>
      <label>Router buffer <select class="pg-in" data-buf><option value="25">0.25 x BDP (shallow)</option><option value="100" selected>1 x BDP</option><option value="400">4 x BDP</option><option value="1600">16 x BDP (bloated)</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Random loss <select class="pg-in" data-loss><option value="0" selected>None</option><option value="1">0.01%</option><option value="10">0.1%</option><option value="100">1%</option></select></label>
      <label>File size <select class="pg-in" data-file><option value="100000">100 KB</option><option value="1000000">1 MB</option><option value="5000000" selected>5 MB</option><option value="50000000">50 MB</option><option value="200000000">200 MB</option></select></label>
      <label>Receive window (rwnd) <select class="pg-in" data-rwnd><option value="65535">64 KB (no scaling)</option><option value="1000000">1 MB</option><option value="6000000" selected>6 MB (autotuned)</option></select></label>
      <label>Seed <input class="pg-in tcp-seed" type="number" min="1" max="999" value="7" data-seed /></label>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label class="tcp-scrub">Round shown <input type="range" min="1" max="1" value="1" data-scrub /> <b class="pg-mono" data-scrubval>1</b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Transfer time</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-time>0 ms</span><span class="pg-note" data-timenote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-2)"><h3>Average throughput</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-tput>0</span><span class="pg-note" data-tputnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Time in slow start</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-ss>0%</span><span class="pg-note" data-ssnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-4)"><h3>Retransmissions</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-retx>0</span><span class="pg-note" data-retxnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-5)"><h3>Queueing delay</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-qd>0 ms</span><span class="pg-note" data-qdnote></span></div>
    </div>
    <svg class="tcp-chart" viewBox="0 0 600 230" role="img" aria-label="Congestion window over time" data-chart>
      <line class="tcp-axis" x1="48" y1="196" x2="590" y2="196"></line>
      <line class="tcp-axis" x1="48" y1="10" x2="48" y2="196"></line>
      <line class="tcp-ref tcp-bdp" data-lbdp x1="48" x2="590"></line>
      <line class="tcp-ref tcp-cap" data-lcap x1="48" x2="590"></line>
      <line class="tcp-ref tcp-rw" data-lrw x1="48" x2="590"></line>
      <path class="tcp-line" data-line d=""></path>
      <path class="tcp-loss" data-marks d=""></path>
      <text class="tcp-txt" data-tbdp x="52" text-anchor="start"></text>
      <text class="tcp-txt" data-tcap x="52" text-anchor="start"></text>
      <text class="tcp-txt" data-trw x="586" text-anchor="end"></text>
      <text class="tcp-txt" data-ymax x="44" y="18" text-anchor="end"></text>
      <text class="tcp-txt" x="44" y="196" text-anchor="end">0</text>
      <text class="tcp-txt" data-xmax x="590" y="214" text-anchor="end"></text>
      <text class="tcp-txt" x="48" y="214" text-anchor="start">0 ms</text>
      <text class="tcp-txt" x="320" y="228" text-anchor="middle">time (cwnd in segments of 1,460 bytes; red marks = loss event)</text>
    </svg>
    <p class="pg-mono tcp-seq" data-seq></p>
    <div class="tcp-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Comparison of the three algorithms with the current settings">
      <table class="tcp-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Algorithm</th><th scope="col">Time</th><th scope="col">Average</th><th scope="col">Retransmits</th><th scope="col">Peak queue delay</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody data-cmp></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: one step is one round trip. cwnd segments go out (capped by rwnd); BDP segments fit in the pipe, the buffer holds the excess and anything beyond BDP + buffer is dropped. A queue adds queue/BDP x RTT to the round. Random loss hits each segment independently (seeded). Three or more later segments arriving means fast retransmit (Reno halves, CUBIC cuts to 0.7); fewer means a timeout of max(200 ms, 3 x RTT) and cwnd 1. CUBIC uses C = 0.4 and beta = 0.7 without HyStart or TCP-friendly mode; BBR-like keeps a 10 round max filter of the delivery rate, runs 3 startup rounds without 25% growth, drains, then cycles pacing gains 1.25, 0.75 and 1 x 6, and ignores loss. Handshake, ACK clocking within a round and delayed ACKs are ignored; the model is for shapes, not for predicting a real link.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue } from '../playground';
  type Algo = 'reno' | 'cubic' | 'bbr';
  interface Params { algo: Algo; mbps: number; rtt: number; bufPct: number; lossBp: number; fileBytes: number; rwndBytes: number; seed: number }
  interface Round { t: number; cwnd: number; sent: number; lost: number; queue: number; qd: number; T: number; phase: string; event: string; delivered: number }
  interface Result { bdp: number; buf: number; total: number; rwnd: number; rounds: Round[]; time: number; retrans: number; done: boolean }

  const MSS = 1460; const IW = 10; const INF = 1e9; const MAXR = 20000;
  const NAMES: Record<Algo, string> = { reno: 'Reno-like AIMD', cubic: 'CUBIC', bbr: 'BBR-like' };

  const BYTES_PER_MBIT_MS = 125; // 1 Mbit/s for 1 ms carries 125 bytes
  const BITS_PER_BYTE = 8, KBIT_PER_MBIT = 1000;
  const TENTHS = 10; // throughput is kept in tenths of a Mbit/s
  const KBPS_PER_TENTH = 100; // bits per ms (kbit/s) in one tenth of a Mbit/s
  const BP = 10000; // loss rate is given in basis points
  const RTO = { minMs: 200, rtts: 3 }; // retransmission timeout: at least 200 ms or 3 RTTs
  const DUPACK_MIN = 4; // fewer delivered segments than this cannot trigger fast retransmit, so it is a timeout
  const BBR = { bwWindow: 10, growthPct: 125, fullRounds: 3, minCwnd: 4, probeStart: 2, gains: [125, 75, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100] }; // max-filter over 10 rounds; startup ends after 3 rounds without 25% growth; probe-bandwidth gain cycle in %
  const CUBIC = { betaNum: 7, betaDen: 10, kScale: 750000000, cNum: 4, cDen: 10000000000 }; // beta 0.7, C 0.4: K = cbrt(wmax * 0.75e9) ms, growth 4 * dt^3 / 1e10 segments
  const ICBRT_HI = 2000000; // search ceiling for the integer cube root
  const PLOT = { x0: 48, w: 542, y0: 196, h: 186, minY: 10, headroom: 1.1 }; // SVG plot box (matches the markup)
  const SEQ_SHOWN = 14; // rounds listed in the cwnd sequence
  const VERDICT = { rwndNum: 9, rwndDen: 10, bloatRtts: 4, ssPct: 90, idlePct: 20 }; // rwnd under 90% of BDP, queue over a quarter RTT, 90% in slow start, under 20% of the link
  // Park-Miller minimal standard LCG
  function makeRng(seed: number) { let s = Math.max(1, seed); return () => { s = (s * 48271) % 2147483647; return s; }; }
  // integer cube root by binary search
  function icbrt(n: number) { let lo = 0; let hi = ICBRT_HI; while (lo < hi) { const m = Math.floor((lo + hi + 1) / 2); if (m * m * m <= n) lo = m; else hi = m - 1; } return lo; }

  function simulate(p: Params): Result {
    const bdp = Math.max(1, Math.floor(p.mbps * BYTES_PER_MBIT_MS * p.rtt / MSS));
    const buf = Math.floor(bdp * p.bufPct / 100);
    const total = Math.ceil(p.fileBytes / MSS);
    const rwnd = Math.max(2, Math.floor(p.rwndBytes / MSS));
    const rto = Math.max(RTO.minMs, RTO.rtts * p.rtt);
    const rnd = makeRng(p.seed);
    const rounds: Round[] = [];
    let remaining = total; let cwnd = IW; let ssthresh = INF; let t = 0; let retrans = 0;
    let wmax = 0; let epoch = -1; let kMs = 0;
    let bw = 0; let fullBw = 0; let fullCnt = 0; let mode = 'startup'; let cyc = 0; const win: number[] = [];
    while (remaining > 0 && rounds.length < MAXR) {
      const sent = Math.min(Math.min(cwnd, rwnd), remaining);
      const queue = Math.min(Math.max(sent - bdp, 0), buf);
      const overflow = Math.max(sent - bdp - buf, 0);
      let rand = 0;
      if (p.lossBp > 0) for (let i = 0; i < sent; i++) if (rnd() % BP < p.lossBp) rand++;
      const lost = Math.min(sent, overflow + rand);
      const qd = Math.floor(queue * p.rtt / bdp);
      let T = p.rtt + qd;
      const delivered = sent - lost;
      const phase = p.algo === 'bbr' ? mode : (cwnd < ssthresh ? 'ss' : 'ca');
      const shown = cwnd; let event = '';
      remaining -= delivered; retrans += lost;
      if (p.algo === 'bbr') {
        const est = Math.floor(delivered * p.rtt / T);
        win.push(est); if (win.length > BBR.bwWindow) win.shift();
        bw = Math.max(...win);
        if (mode === 'startup') {
          if (bw * 100 >= fullBw * BBR.growthPct) { fullBw = bw; fullCnt = 0; } else fullCnt++;
          if (fullCnt >= BBR.fullRounds) { mode = 'drain'; cwnd = Math.max(BBR.minCwnd, bw); }
          else cwnd = Math.min(2 * cwnd, 2 * Math.max(bw, IW));
        } else if (mode === 'drain') { mode = 'probe'; cyc = BBR.probeStart; cwnd = Math.max(BBR.minCwnd, bw); }
        else { const g = BBR.gains[cyc]; cyc = (cyc + 1) % BBR.gains.length; cwnd = Math.max(BBR.minCwnd, Math.floor(bw * g / 100)); }
      } else if (lost > 0) {
        wmax = cwnd;
        ssthresh = Math.max(2, p.algo === 'cubic' ? Math.floor(cwnd * CUBIC.betaNum / CUBIC.betaDen) : Math.floor(cwnd / 2));
        if (sent - lost < DUPACK_MIN) { event = 'timeout'; T += rto; cwnd = 1; epoch = -1; }
        else { event = 'fast'; cwnd = ssthresh; epoch = t + T; kMs = icbrt(wmax * CUBIC.kScale); }
      } else if (cwnd < rwnd) {
        if (cwnd < ssthresh) cwnd = Math.min(cwnd * 2, Math.max(ssthresh, 2));
        else if (p.algo === 'reno') cwnd += 1;
        else {
          if (epoch < 0) { epoch = t; kMs = icbrt(wmax * CUBIC.kScale); }
          const dt = (t + T - epoch) + p.rtt - kMs; const a = Math.abs(dt);
          const c = Math.floor(CUBIC.cNum * a * a * a / CUBIC.cDen);
          const target = dt < 0 ? wmax - c : wmax + c;
          if (target > cwnd) cwnd += Math.min(target - cwnd, Math.floor(cwnd / 2));
        }
      }
      rounds.push({ t, cwnd: shown, sent, lost, queue, qd, T, phase, event, delivered });
      t += T;
    }
    return { bdp, buf, total, rwnd, rounds, time: t, retrans, done: remaining <= 0 };
  }

  function stats(r: Result, upto: number) {
    let ss = 0; let time = 0; let maxQ = 0; let qSum = 0; let deliv = 0; let lost = 0; let timeouts = 0; let fast = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < upto && i < r.rounds.length; i++) {
      const x = r.rounds[i];
      time += x.T; if (x.phase === 'ss' || x.phase === 'startup') ss += x.T;
      if (x.qd > maxQ) maxQ = x.qd; qSum += x.qd * x.T; deliv += x.delivered; lost += x.lost;
      if (x.event === 'timeout') timeouts++; if (x.event === 'fast') fast++;
    }
    return { time, ssPct: time ? Math.floor(ss * 100 / time) : 0, maxQ, avgQ: time ? Math.floor(qSum / time) : 0, lost, timeouts, fast,
      mbps10: time ? Math.floor(deliv * MSS * BITS_PER_BYTE / time / KBPS_PER_TENTH) : 0, rounds: Math.min(upto, r.rounds.length) };
  }

  const fmtMs = (ms: number) => (ms >= 10000 ? (ms / 1000).toFixed(1) + ' s' : ms.toLocaleString('en-US') + ' ms');
  const fmtMbps = (m10: number) => (m10 / TENTHS).toFixed(1) + ' Mbit/s';

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-tcp]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const setText = (s: string, v: string) => { q(s).textContent = v; };
    const rowCells: Record<string, HTMLElement[]> = {};
    const cmp = q<HTMLElement>('[data-cmp]');
    (['reno', 'cubic', 'bbr'] as Algo[]).forEach((a) => {
      const tr = document.createElement('tr'); const th = document.createElement('th'); th.scope = 'row'; th.textContent = NAMES[a]; tr.appendChild(th);
      rowCells[a] = [0, 1, 2, 3].map(() => { const td = document.createElement('td'); tr.appendChild(td); return td; });
      cmp.appendChild(tr);
    });
    const defaults: Record<string, string> = { '[data-algo]': 'reno', '[data-mbps]': '100', '[data-rtt]': '80', '[data-buf]': '100', '[data-loss]': '0', '[data-file]': '5000000', '[data-rwnd]': '6000000', '[data-seed]': '7' };
    let result: Result | null = null; let raf = 0;

    function params(algo: Algo): Params {
      return { algo, mbps: val('[data-mbps]'), rtt: val('[data-rtt]'), bufPct: val('[data-buf]'), lossBp: val('[data-loss]'), fileBytes: val('[data-file]'), rwndBytes: val('[data-rwnd]'), seed: Math.max(1, Math.floor(val('[data-seed]')) || 1) };
    }
    function recompute() {
      const algo = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-algo]').value as Algo;
      setText('[data-rttval]', String(val('[data-rtt]')));
      result = simulate(params(algo));
      const scrub = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-scrub]');
      scrub.max = String(result.rounds.length); scrub.value = String(result.rounds.length);
      (['reno', 'cubic', 'bbr'] as Algo[]).forEach((a) => {
        const r = a === algo ? result! : simulate(params(a)); const s = stats(r, r.rounds.length); const c = rowCells[a];
        c[0].textContent = fmtMs(r.time) + (r.done ? '' : ' (stopped)'); c[1].textContent = fmtMbps(s.mbps10); c[2].textContent = String(r.retrans); c[3].textContent = s.maxQ + ' ms';
      });
      schedule();
    }
    function schedule() { if (!raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(() => { raf = 0; draw(); }); }

    function draw() {
      if (!result) return;
      const r = result; const p = params(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-algo]').value as Algo);
      const upto = Math.max(1, Math.min(r.rounds.length, val('[data-scrub]')));
      const s = stats(r, upto); const last = r.rounds[upto - 1]; const finished = upto >= r.rounds.length;
      setText('[data-scrubval]', `${upto} of ${r.rounds.length}`);
      const idealMs = Math.floor(p.fileBytes * BITS_PER_BYTE / (p.mbps * KBIT_PER_MBIT));
      setText('[data-time]', fmtMs(s.time)); setText('[data-timenote]', finished ? (r.done ? `${s.rounds} round trips; ideal at line rate ${fmtMs(idealMs)}` : `stopped after ${MAXR.toLocaleString('en-US')} rounds, not finished`) : `so far, after round ${upto}`);
      setText('[data-tput]', fmtMbps(s.mbps10)); setText('[data-tputnote]', `${Math.floor(s.mbps10 / TENTHS * 100 / p.mbps)}% of the ${p.mbps >= 1000 ? '1 Gbit/s' : p.mbps + ' Mbit/s'} link`);
      setText('[data-ss]', s.ssPct + '%'); setText('[data-ssnote]', p.algo === 'bbr' ? 'BBR startup phase' : 'before the first loss or ssthresh');
      setText('[data-retx]', String(s.lost)); setText('[data-retxnote]', `${s.fast} fast retransmit, ${s.timeouts} timeout events`);
      setText('[data-qd]', s.maxQ + ' ms'); setText('[data-qdnote]', `peak; average ${s.avgQ} ms on top of ${p.rtt} ms RTT`);

      let maxC = 1; for (let i = 0; i < upto; i++) if (r.rounds[i].cwnd > maxC) maxC = r.rounds[i].cwnd;
      const yMax = Math.max(maxC, r.bdp, PLOT.minY) * PLOT.headroom; const full = Math.max(1, r.time);
      const X = (t: number) => PLOT.x0 + (t / full) * PLOT.w; const Y = (c: number) => PLOT.y0 - (c / yMax) * PLOT.h;
      let d = ''; let m = '';
      for (let i = 0; i < upto; i++) {
        const x = r.rounds[i];
        d += (i === 0 ? 'M' : 'L') + X(x.t).toFixed(1) + ' ' + Y(x.cwnd).toFixed(1) + 'L' + X(x.t + x.T).toFixed(1) + ' ' + Y(x.cwnd).toFixed(1);
        if (x.lost > 0) { const cx = X(x.t + x.T / 2); const cy = Y(x.cwnd); m += `M${(cx - 3).toFixed(1)} ${cy.toFixed(1)}a3 3 0 1 0 6 0a3 3 0 1 0 -6 0`; }
      }
      q('[data-line]').setAttribute('d', d); q('[data-marks]').setAttribute('d', m);
      const place = (line: string, text: string, v: number, label: string) => {
        const el = q(line); const tx = q(text); const show = v <= yMax && v > 0;
        el.setAttribute('visibility', show ? 'visible' : 'hidden'); tx.setAttribute('visibility', show ? 'visible' : 'hidden');
        const y = Y(v).toFixed(1); el.setAttribute('y1', y); el.setAttribute('y2', y); tx.setAttribute('y', String(Number(y) - 3)); tx.textContent = label;
      };
      place('[data-lbdp]', '[data-tbdp]', r.bdp, `BDP ${r.bdp}`);
      place('[data-lcap]', '[data-tcap]', r.bdp + r.buf, `BDP + buffer ${r.bdp + r.buf}`);
      place('[data-lrw]', '[data-trw]', r.rwnd, `rwnd ${r.rwnd}`);
      setText('[data-ymax]', String(Math.floor(yMax))); setText('[data-xmax]', fmtMs(r.time));
      q('[data-chart]').setAttribute('aria-label', `Congestion window over ${fmtMs(r.time)}: ${NAMES[p.algo]}, peak cwnd ${maxC} segments, BDP ${r.bdp} segments`);
      const seq: string[] = []; for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(upto, SEQ_SHOWN); i++) seq.push(r.rounds[i].cwnd + (r.rounds[i].event === 'timeout' ? '!' : r.rounds[i].lost > 0 ? '*' : ''));
      setText('[data-seq]', `cwnd per round: ${seq.join(' ')}${upto > SEQ_SHOWN ? ' ...' : ''}   (* loss, ! timeout; round ${upto} phase: ${last.phase})`);
      const verdict = !r.done ? 'The transfer did not finish within the round limit; try a larger BDP (more bandwidth or RTT) or a smaller file.'
        : r.rwnd * VERDICT.rwndDen < r.bdp * VERDICT.rwndNum ? `The receive window (${r.rwnd} segments) is smaller than the BDP (${r.bdp}): throughput is capped at rwnd / RTT whatever cwnd would allow.`
        : s.avgQ * VERDICT.bloatRtts > p.rtt ? `The queue averages ${s.avgQ} ms (peak ${s.maxQ} ms) on top of the ${p.rtt} ms RTT: that is bufferbloat.`
        : s.ssPct >= VERDICT.ssPct && finished ? `The transfer ended almost entirely inside slow start (${s.ssPct}% of the time): the round-trip count, not the bandwidth, decided the time.`
        : p.algo !== 'bbr' && s.mbps10 * 100 < p.mbps * TENTHS * VERDICT.idlePct && p.lossBp > 0 ? 'Random loss is read as congestion: each loss halves a small window, so the link stays mostly idle.'
        : 'The window tracks the path: compare the three rows in the table.';
      setText('[data-verdict]', finished ? verdict : 'Replaying: totals above cover rounds 1 to ' + upto + ' only.');
    }

    root.querySelectorAll('select, input[type=range], input[type=number]').forEach((el) => {
      if (el === q('[data-scrub]')) el.addEventListener('input', schedule); else el.addEventListener('input', recompute);
    });
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      for (const k of Object.keys(defaults)) q<HTMLInputElement>(k).value = defaults[k];
      recompute();
    });
    recompute();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .tcp .tcp-seed { width: 5em; }
  .playground .tcp .tcp-scrub { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .playground .tcp .tcp-chart { width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 300px; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
  .playground .tcp .tcp-axis { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; }
  .playground .tcp .tcp-ref { stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .playground .tcp .tcp-bdp { stroke: var(--role-3); }
  .playground .tcp .tcp-cap { stroke: var(--bad); }
  .playground .tcp .tcp-rw { stroke: var(--muted); }
